\section*{Conventions}
Scalars are italic ($x$, $t$), vectors bold lowercase ($\vect{p}$), matrices bold
uppercase ($\mat{A}$), sets calligraphic ($\mathcal{S}$), and estimates carry a hat
($\hat{x}$). % Adapt to the book; every macro of textbook.sty appears below.

